      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:psflavianus.encomium.budge:24-42",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲉⲣϣⲁⲛⲡⲙⲟⲩ ⲅⲁⲣ ⲡⲱⲣϫ ⲛⲧⲉⲯⲩⲭⲏ ⲉⲃⲟⲗ ⲙⲡⲥⲱⲙⲁ ⲉⲩⲙⲟⲩⲧⲉ ⲉⲣⲟϥ ϫⲉⲕⲱⲱⲛⲥ · ⲉϥⲟ ⲛ**ⲥϯⲃⲱⲱⲛ** ·",
      "english": "Now when death hath separated the soul from the body they call the body a 'corpse', and it giveth forth foetidness.",
      "source": "On the Soul and Body",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:psathanasius.soul_body.budge:1-91",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    }
